{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "kind": "standard",
  "organization": "ScaleDock",
  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers OpenFGA, the CNCF relationship-based access control system inspired by Zanzibar: the modeling language in DSL and JSON (types, relations, direct relationship type restrictions, usersets, type-bound public access, or, and, but not, from tupleset rewrites, nesting), conditions with CEL expressions, contextual tuples, modular models with fga.mod and extend type, relationship tuples and the API (Write, Read, ReadChanges, Check, BatchCheck, Expand, ListObjects, StreamedListObjects, ListUsers, authorization model ids, consistency preferences), .fga.yaml tests with the CLI, and modeling patterns for roles, groups, hierarchies, public access, custom roles and blocklists. Version lines: schema 1.1 is current, schema 1.0 is legacy, schema 1.2 (modular models) is current in its own family, and OpenFGA server v1.21 is current in the server family; pinned to openfga.dev at fb53597, openfga/api at c0650ce and openfga/language at f558baa. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions, the modeling language, conditions and modules, tuples and the API, and testing and patterns.",
